<main id="main" class="wide page-space"><div class="page-intro"><span class="eyebrow muted-eyebrow">YOUR INFORMATION MATTERS</span><h1>Privacy & responsible use</h1><p>Application notice version 2026-10-27. The school or organisation operating this deployment must provide its contact details, safeguarding arrangements and applicable privacy policy before enrolling learners.</p></div><div class="panel prose narrow-panel">
<h2>What we collect and why</h2><p>Your account contains your name, email, optional grade and self-reported school, and a securely hashed password. You choose whether to add subjects, grades, skills, preferences, guidance needs and ambitions. The application saves your interest assessments, recommendation history, favourite items and career plans so you can review changes. Guidance uses transparent weighted matching; it is not a trained prediction of success, a diagnosis, or an admission decision.</p>
<h2>School and educator access</h2><p>Your self-reported school does not give anyone access to your records. Administrators must confirm school membership. A teacher can view your guidance profile and write brief counselling notes only when you grant that teacher permission in <a href="account.php">Account & privacy</a>, and both accounts belong to the same confirmed school. You can revoke permission at any time. A role or school reassignment revokes old grants. Notes are limited to career guidance and should not contain medical, family or other sensitive information.</p><p>School statistics use the latest assessment per learner. Groups smaller than five are suppressed; larger counts are displayed in bands of five. Administrators manage access and verified content and can see account contact details, but the administration interface does not expose individual learner profiles or assessment answers.</p>
<h2>AI assistant</h2><p>The application's own recommendation service receives your question and the minimum context needed to explain your career guidance. Chat history is not stored by this interface. External generative AI is disabled by default. Do not enter identifying, medical or other private information in chat. Operators must assess and document any third-party processing before enabling an external provider.</p>
<h2>Children and consent</h2><p>This service is intended for high school learners, who may be minors. School or guardian permission may be required under the operator's policies and applicable rules. A registration checkbox is an acknowledgement of this notice, not independently verified guardian consent. The operator must establish an appropriate consent process before real school deployment. Educator sharing remains optional within the application.</p>
<h2>History, retention and deletion</h2><p>New assessments and profile updates preserve earlier guidance history. You can download your information as JSON, including guidance notes about you, in <a href="account.php">Account & privacy</a>. You can also permanently delete your active account and associated learner records after confirming your password. Administrators must first transfer their responsibilities.</p><p>Expired recovery tokens and old rate-limit records can be removed by operator maintenance. The supplied maintenance policy defaults to removing guidance notes and audit entries older than 365 days; operators can configure these periods and must schedule the maintenance job. It does not silently delete your assessment history. Backups are managed outside the application: operators must publish their retention period, encrypt them, restrict access and ensure deleted accounts are not restored into active service. Minimal audit records are de-identified when an account is deleted.</p>
<h2>Security and offline reading</h2><p>Signed-in pages use private, no-store cache headers. Only public reference information is eligible for offline caching. Recovery links contain random, short-lived tokens; only their hashes are stored. Password resets and access changes invalidate previous sessions. Keep exported reports and downloaded data private and sign out on shared devices.</p>
<h2>Information quality</h2><p>Career reference data includes international information and is not a verified Lesotho labour-market forecast. Programme, scholarship and admission records show their sources and verification scope. Partial requirements remain uncertain even if the listed subject prerequisites are met. Institutions decide admission and funding.</p>
<h2>Contact and support</h2><p><?php $support=env_value('SUPPORT_EMAIL'); if(filter_var($support,FILTER_VALIDATE_EMAIL)): ?>Contact <a href="mailto:<?= e($support) ?>"><?= e($support) ?></a> about access, correction, safeguarding or deletion.<?php else: ?>Contact your school or the organisation running this deployment. The operator has not yet configured a support email address and must do so before inviting real learners.<?php endif; ?></p>
</div></main><?php page_end(); ?>
